# Cross-Chat Verbatim Recall Test: 440 AI Models

## Method

We gave the system **440 total AI-model items** in one chat, organized into five provider lists:

- 71 Z.AI models
- 33 Anthropic models
- 138 Qwen models
- OpenAI models
- Google models

Each item was saved in the context library with its provider, model name, description, pricing, and other list information.

After saving the lists, we opened a **completely new chat** for each test. We did not paste the original lists into those new chats. Instead, we asked for one specific provider list and requested it verbatim.

For each separate chat, ask for a specific list:

“Give me the 71 Z.AI models verbatim.”

“Give me the 33 Anthropic AI models verbatim.”

“Give me the 138 Qwen AI models verbatim.”

“Give me the OpenAI AI models verbatim.”

“Give me the Google AI models verbatim.”

The process is:

1. Put the complete lists into one chat.
2. Save each list to the context library.
3. Open a brand-new chat.
4. Ask for one provider’s list using the corresponding prompt.
5. Compare the response with the original using a deterministic verbatim checker.
6. Open another brand-new chat.
7. Repeat the process for the next provider.
8. Continue until every list has been tested.

The test was not performed by asking all five questions in one conversation. Each question was tested in its **own separate, brand-new chat**.

All five retrieval tests achieved perfect verbatim recall.

**Total tested: 440 AI-model items across five provider lists.**



